dtbuilder(1): its NAME line in the form whatis reads.

The page's NAME heading is "Name" and its line separates the name from
the purpose with \(mi and sets CDE in a smaller size; whatis and man -k
read "name \- text" under ".SH NAME", as patch 30 gives the other pages.

--- a/programs/dtappbuilder/src/ab/dtbuilder.1
+++ b/programs/dtappbuilder/src/ab/dtbuilder.1
@@ -48,8 +48,8 @@
 .\"--- or:
 .\"--- dtgather \(mi gather application files for presentation by the Application Manager
 .\"---
-.SH Name
-dtbuilder \(mi the \s-1CDE\s+1 Application Builder
+.SH NAME
+dtbuilder \- the CDE Application Builder
 .\"---
 .\"----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 .\"--- SYNOPSIS
